    "submission": "update-stage27.json",
    "summary": "Last sourced lead of the run, registered as a conditional boundary rather than a claim (valid:true).\n\nWhat source establishes: `appendConfigurationEntry` chooses the entry format from the leader's protocol version alone — below 2 it appends the deprecated remove-peer entry carrying `encodePeers` output (raft.go:1219-1233) — and `encodePeers` gathers only servers whose suffrage is Voter, with the explicit comment that other suffrage types are not supported by that format (configuration.go:311-327). The receiving side is symmetric: a deprecated entry is decoded by `decodePeers`, which reconstructs every server as a voter (configuration.go:330-352), and the same encoder also fills the peers field returned to below-2 voters (raft.go:1620-1622). `nextConfiguration` had computed the full configuration and `checkConfiguration` only insists on at least one voter, so a non-voter or staging entry would not stop the append — it simply could not be represented in the written entry.\n\nWhat is not established, and why the question stays paused: reachability of the precondition. Non-voter and staging entries can only enter through the versioned configuration format or a snapshot from a member that used it, so the candidate paths are a deliberate downgrade of a running member, a mixed-version cluster where the older node wins an election, and a snapshot restored from a newer member — none of which this turn constructed or found traversed in source. The registered discriminator is to append one membership change on such a leader and compare the decoded entry with the configuration the change requested; a defect requires a delivered entry missing a server the requested configuration contained. Counterevidence keeps the scope honest: a cluster that only ever ran protocol 1 cannot hold such entries, and `checkConfiguration` still guarantees at least one voter, so the possible loss is of non-voting members, not of quorum. A behaviour describing the lossy encoder, the protocol-version branch and the matching decoder is recorded, with Chinese report fields omitted since the question is unresolved rather than answered."
